// usfm-booklet — the first two chapters of John set as a pocket booklet. The page is a quarter of a US Letter
// sheet (4.25 x 5.5 in); \arrange booklet imposes the pages two-up, in saddle-stitch folding order, onto
// half-letter-landscape (8.5 x 5.5 in) sheets. Print double-sided, fold each sheet down the middle, and nest and
// staple them, and the pages read in order — a pocket booklet folded from half-letter paper. (For A-series paper
// use `\geometry paper:a6 top:10mm left:10mm right:10mm bottom:16mm footskip:5mm` instead — A6 pages on A5.)

\use{usfm}

\usehyphenation{en-us}

\geometry paperwidth:4.25in paperheight:5.5in top:0.4in left:0.4in right:0.4in bottom:0.6in footskip:0.2in
\arrange booklet

\usfm{john12.usfm}

\vfill\eject
